From 1859fe3faa2b82a759c965ab0e958dab6b5e6019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:40:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Exercise the development runtime with real fork recovery

Add an isolated integration target and root-authorized fixture header copied from the immutable complete-block corpus at f93ea73fd. Validate an explicitly configured V4 runtime through its public API; source branches are complete-block disk commits and only replacement bodies enter the three-slot volatile pool. No existing golden bytes or production sources change.

Cover heavier-fork selection, stale availability and indexed-revision observations, insertion during bounded scans, exact invalid-middle source restoration with an emptied pool, separate terminal receipt acknowledgement and causal invalidation, and inconclusive execution pause/retry/reopen with identical journal bytes. Check bounded diagnostics against expected roots, monetary bytes, CoinEntries, proofs and active ancestry.

Inject a reported failure after an actually successful synchronous write, require cached authority to disappear, then reopen and resume from the observed durable first-detach checkpoint. Exercise callback Busy guards, capacity refusal and both availability/context counter exhaustion before mutation or wraparound. Usage remains per component, with at most one recovery call per tick rather than a fictitious combined VM budget.

The final strict Debug and targeted AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suites pass against exact runtime d3e86735b (root 86676b778). The runtime owner independently passed Release and is confirming the final equality assertions before promotion. Commit only the four authorized test/fixture/recipe/documentation files; runtime sources are borrowed build dependencies and shared CMake registration remains root-owned.
